# N2/P13 Results - Deferred C-Backed Pair Exactification

## Status

P13 is complete. It preserved the frozen P12/P11/P8 dispatch policy, the `0.80` cutoff, P6 folding backend, Gate-P family, natural EPFL controls, and timing endpoints. P13 changed only pair telemetry: source construction appends canonical packed pair keys, while exact distinct-pair and multiplicity work is deferred to C-backed builtins at dispatch.

Mandatory P12/P13 invariance passed on **332/332** frozen policy cases, and fresh fuzz passed **1000/1000**. The independent verifier reports PASS.

## Gate-P primary endpoint

| Comparison | Case-balanced geomean | 95% bootstrap CI | Workload-weighted | Wins |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P13 / direct, source-inclusive | **1.016459x** | **0.950719-1.063606** | **0.980269x** | 3/36 |
| P13 / P12, source-inclusive | **0.996897x** | **0.990522-1.003201** | **0.997617x** | 20/36 |
| P13 / direct, source build+dispatch | **1.271686x** | **1.243704-1.298599** | **1.286860x** | 0/36 |
| P13 / P12, source build+dispatch | **0.992477x** | **0.980345-1.003794** | **0.994002x** | 19/36 |
| P13 / direct, selected compiler | **0.957886x** | **0.853190-1.037952** | **0.814362x** | 10/36 |

The preregistered **direct-crossover criterion did not pass**. P13 remains about **1.65% above direct case-balanced**, and the confidence interval crosses 1. The workload-weighted endpoint remains below direct at **0.980269x**, about **1.97% faster** in aggregate, but this is still a secondary endpoint.

Against simultaneous P12, P13's point estimate is only **0.31% faster source-inclusive** and **0.75% faster in source build+dispatch**. Both confidence intervals include 1, so the deferred-pair implementation is not a clear improvement over P12 under the preregistered criteria.

Median-of-case-median Gate-P source build+dispatch was approximately **47.4 us direct**, **60.5 us P12**, and **60.2 us P13**. Whole-pipeline medians were approximately **234.4 us**, **247.0 us**, and **246.7 us**.

## Deferred pair behavior

Only **7/36** Gate-P cases required Stage-2 exact multiplicity counting with `_collections._count_elements`; **6/36** required the reuse scan, with **1** early reuse abort.

Thus P13 successfully removes the per-binary Python pair-count dictionary from the construction path. The fact that timing changes only marginally indicates that the remaining cost is not primarily Python-level count updates. Packing/storing one pair identity per binary node plus the dispatch-time exact distinct-pair pass remains enough to preserve most of the telemetry tax.

